rota lap 4330, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; listening for the silence where a claim used to be led straight to my own lane, where main.rye had gone quiet about a model the module had widened past
think REDS %589 stood OPEN with one sentence holding it shut -- reconciling main.rye rewrites a shipped on-disk record -- written in the ledger row, in the witness header, and in the scan header alike
think my own elder lap had already landed Weave.to_v1 and said the blocker was gone; what it had not done was port the CLI, so the claim stayed a claim
think the port is the crux under Lindy-first: the CLI is what a person runs, and one declaration cannot drift from itself
think the honest test of does-the-port-move-the-record is not an argument, it is two binaries and a content-addressed store
obs baseline binary built in 1.9s, so the elder behavior was available to compare against rather than to remember
obs elder and ported binaries ran the same six edits -- insert, delete, append, prepend, empty the file, refill it -- and every digest matched: twelve commit and weave names, all thirteen store files
obs a matching digest under a content-addressed store IS a byte-identical record, which is the strongest available answer and needs no further argument
obs the mid-file insert reads as a delete plus an append in BOTH binaries, so it is the module's documented append-at-end semantics rather than a regression I introduced -- checked before reporting it
obs the cure was deleting a copy rather than reconciling one, which the scan's own comment already named as the outcome it welcomes; copies fell 2 to 1
obs booking %589 made it foldable and the fold freed 1,740 bytes, headroom 24 -> 1,764 -- yet rows_that_fit is still 0 against a median row of 2,702, so DIFFUSER's gate stands unrelieved
obs the fold follows the work rather than drives it: the row is BOOKED because its shipped instance is repaired and its remainder is one ratcheted copy, and the pin relief is a consequence
obs against myself -- I wrote my baseline binary to /tmp minutes after reading the baton clause naming that exact habit, and moved to .lap/ only once the port was written
obs against myself, the second: I launched the cold roster pass and then edited for half an hour while it ran, which the card forbids in five words -- hold still while it runs. tree_moved=yes caught it, so that reading was not evidence and I reran hot, holding still, for tree_moved=no
obs the hot pass reads 190 green, 3 red, and none of the three is mine: standing_equipment is derivative of the other two, stash_record is %636's inherited gate, and seed_link I proved not mine by running its scan at HEAD in a throwaway worktree -- identical count, identical gated line
obs seed_link is a LIVE red booked nowhere: README.md links context/BHAKTA_STYLE.md, a room the seed does not carry, and the ratchet reads 850 against a ceiling of 848. It went red at 14:29 with 3688723c1, a peer's front-door commit, and appears in neither REDS nor ITINERARY -- which is the deadlocked pin biting for real, since no ship could book it
obs so the fold's relief is not abstract: headroom went 24 -> 1,764, which is room a short row now has, and the red that needs one arrived while there was none
obs the ITINERARY card is full: my block at its honest length ran 518 bytes past what the card had room for, and eight cuts brought it to 40,951 of 40,960
